387 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (STEP 1: Start with C or Am. Fill up all the bars of the 16-bar template below with chords from the matrix. It is ok to choose randomly; often that's how you start the process. \(If you want to create more of a pop song structure, copy bars 1-4 into bars 5-8\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (STEP 2: Follow the arrows. If you use a secondary dominant, you must resolve in the direction of the arrow. \(For Example, if you use a F#7, the next chord must be a B7 and the next one must be a Em\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 160 0 R
/E (STEP 3: If using a red followed by a green chord, feel free to include both in the same bar. \(no need to hold each one for an entire bar\). )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
